//! Recursive descent and operator-precedence parser for XCL source code.
//!
//! # Overview
//!
//! The parser takes the linear sequence of [`TokenWithText`](xcl_toolchain::lexer::TokenWithText)
//! generated by [`lex`](xcl_toolchain::lexer::lex) and constructs an Abstract Syntax Tree
//! represented by a [`Vec<AstNode>`](xcl_toolchain::ast::AstNode).
//!
//! # Parsing Strategy
//!
//! * **Statements**: Parsed using recursive descent with lookahead. Handled constructs include
//!   variable assignments (`$x = 42`), loop statements (`for`, `while`), branch statements (`if`/`else`),
//!   function definitions (`name($args) { ... }`), custom type definitions (`Point = { ... }`),
//!   trait implementations (`Human is Walk { ... }`), and `defer` cleanup blocks.
//! * **Expressions**: Parsed using Pratt / precedence climbing to correctly resolve operator
//!   precedence and associativity for arithmetic, comparisons, logical operations, and pipeline (`|>`) chaining.
//!
//! # Layout
//!
//! | File | Holds |
//! |---|---|
//! | `mod.rs` | `Parser` state, cursor/error/recovery helpers, `parse` / `parse_recover` |
//! | `stmt.rs` | programs, assignments, control flow, functions, domain expansion |
//! | `expr.rs` | the precedence chain from `expr` down to `unary`, plus postfix and pipelines |
//! | `primary.rs` | literals, arrays, maps, grouping, and argument lookaheads |
//! | `ty.rs` | type expressions (`parse_type`) |
//!
//! Every method except the entry points is `pub(super)`: the split is for
//! readers, not a public API.
//!
//! # Examples
//!
//! Parsing source code into an AST:
//!
//! ```
//! use xcl_toolchain::compiler::lexer::lex;
//! use xcl_toolchain::compiler::parser::parse;
//! use xcl_toolchain::compiler::ast::AstNode;
//!
//! let source = "$total = 100 + 50;";
//! let tokens = lex(source, "main.xcl");
//! let ast = parse(&tokens, source);
//!
//! assert_eq!(ast.len(), 1);
//! match &ast[0] {
//!     AstNode::Assign { name, .. } => assert_eq!(name, "total"),
//!     _ => panic!("Expected assignment"),
//! }
//! ```

